ent":"H-1-5207","date":"2026-03","file":"kodak-vision3-250d.pdf","url":"https://www.kodak.com/content/products-brochures/motion-picture/KODAK-VISION3-250D-5207-7207-technical-information.pdf","sha256":"70adb298a7aabb285d986b720e07c87c27eb2361f0925aea2b15903c08282e16"},"notes":["Read from the current raster copy (H-1-5207, revised 3-26, kodak-vision3-250d.pdf), the only copy available; hints were placed on the printed curves by hand (columns and rows of ink located from the rendered page), so every trace follows the plotted line within about 0.02 of the axis unit.","Exposure indexes printed: daylight (5500 K), metal halide, HMI and Kino Flo 55 at 250 with no filter; tungsten (3000 K or 3200 K) at 64 with the Wratten 2 / 80A filter. The curves are for 5500 K daylight, 1/50 s, so balance is daylight and iso 250.","Characteristic curves: the top axis (log exposure, lux-seconds) is printed with nine rounded labels -3.7, -3.1, -2.5, -1.9, -1.3, -0.7, -0.1, 0.5, 1.1 (0.6 apart, one label per 2 stops); the bottom axis gives camera stops -8 to +8 over the same width. x is that printed axis, -3.7 at the left frame and 1.1 at the right frame (4.8 log units, 16 stops). Densitometry: Status M.","No Log H Ref or grey-card density table is printed, so log_h_ref is null.","Spectral sensitivity: effective exposure 0.02 s, ECN-2, Status M, density 0.2 above D-min; y is log sensitivity (reciprocal exposure in erg/cm2) as printed. The yellow-forming layer (b) is drawn from about 360 to 520 nm, the magenta-forming layer (g) from 400 to 600 nm (it starts at 0.6 at 400 nm, dips to about 0.35 at 440 nm and then rises, so the magenta curve has a second, low piece at the left), the cyan-forming layer (r) from 530 to 700 nm; the lines stop where Kodak stops them. The layers cross near 490 nm (yellow with magenta) and 588 nm (magenta with cyan).","Spectral dye density: ECN-2, D-mins subtracted, diffuse density; the cyan, magenta and yellow dye curves are peak-normalised (peak 1.0), mid is the Midscale Neutral curve and min the dashed Minimum Density curve (from 400 to about 790 nm, the line stops before 800). The cyan dye and the midscale neutral curve touch near 625 nm and again merge between 750 and 775 nm; beyond that the neutral curve is read as the upper one, as on the 200T, 500T and 50D sheets. Magenta dips slightly below 0 near 440 nm.","Grain: the sheet gives diffuse rms granularity curves only (48 micrometre aperture, ECN-2; Sigma D scale on the right, multiply by 1000), no single printed value, so grain is null. Read by eye, Sigma D is roughly 0.005 to 0.008 for the green and red records (rms about 5 to 8) and 0.007 to 0.012 for the blue record, depending on density.","Print film: none is named on the sheet; LAD values are said to be specific to each print or duplicating film."],"print":"kodak-2383"}